course: dictionary
lesson: 8480
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word sample can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. Ask yourself: is this a thing, or something someone does?
explain: As a noun, a sample is a small part that shows what the rest is like. «Pool test kits compare the colour of a water sample with drops added to a colour card.» The little bit of water tells us about all the water in the pool.
explain: As a verb, to sample means to try a little of something. «Many call those notes the first computer program» is not about samples, but a free sample in a shop is a small taste or amount given so you can try it. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: A sample is a small amount or part of something that shows what the rest is like.
fact: A free sample is a small amount of a product given to try.
fact: In science and maths, a sample is a group chosen from a larger group to be tested or studied.
fact: To sample means to try or taste a little of something.
fact: In music, a sample is a short piece of sound that is reused in a new song.
exercise: «Doctors take a blood sample to check your health.» What is a sample here? | *A small amount of blood that shows what the rest is like | A bandage for a cut | A kind of doctor | A hospital bed
exercise: Maya says, «I'll sample the cheese at the market.» What does sample mean here? | To buy the whole cheese | *To try a little of it | To count how many cheeses there are | To throw the cheese away
exercise: The new song uses a short piece of an old tune. In music, what is that piece called? | A lullaby | A choir | *A sample | A piano lesson
test: The shop gives out free samples of yoghurt. What is a free sample? | A type of shop that sells yoghurt | A large box of yoghurt you must pay for | *A small amount of a product given to try | A yoghurt recipe
test: «A survey asked a sample of pupils what they like, to learn about the whole school.» What is a sample here? | A school trip | *A small group chosen from a bigger group to be studied | The head teacher's office | A list of rules for the school
exam: Which sentence uses sample as a verb? | *Please sample the soup before you decide | A free sample came in the post | The sample was very small | The water sample was tested in the lab
